invariant: INV-16
file: srv_flight.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: the frozen digest from the cookie is compared with memcmp instead of
  ct_memeq. memcmp returns at the first differing byte, so a client that
  can repeat a retry learns how many leading bytes of the digest its second
  ClientHello matched. srv_cookie.h states that this comparison runs over
  all SHA256_LEN bytes for the reason the MAC's does, and every answer stays
  the same, which is why the rule and not a test catches it, the way
  srv-cookie-memcmp is caught.

--- old
    if (!ct_memeq(frozen, ch->frozen, sizeof frozen)) {
--- new
    if (memcmp(frozen, ch->frozen, sizeof frozen) != 0) {
